Pi Tech Lab / ScholarPi: two licenses

Copyright (c) 2026 Ali Vafadar Yengejeh (Pi Tech Lab).

This repository holds two kinds of work, under two licenses.

1. The science engines: open source, under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only
   (back/LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt; SPDX: AGPL-3.0-only). Anyone may use, study, change and share them. Anyone who
   runs a changed version for users over a network must offer those users the source of their version (AGPL
   section 13).

     back/api.py             the whole server in one file (owner, 2026-10-13): it holds the science
                                engines (the Pi-Index scoring rubric, the assessment pipeline, routing to the
                                panel's models, scientometrics, attribution, security checks, bibliographic
                                extraction and lookups, the shared HTTP client, reception diagnostics, the
                                proof-of-research ledger), and so the file as a whole, the platform code
                                merged into it included, is AGPL-3.0-only
     back/rust/numbers/              the constants (pi, e, phi, gamma) in Rust, and front/numbers.wasm built from it

   Each of these carries an SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only header. Inside back/api.py, banners
   name the module each part came from; the engines listed above were the open ones before the merge.

2. Everything else, including the website and its design: proprietary, all rights reserved
   (back/LICENSES/LicenseRef-PiTechLab-Proprietary.txt). That is the front end and its look, the superellipse and
   glass interface, the SuperAI language and its engines (back/rust/superai, back/rust/pifront, front/super/), the
   site's program, and the platform that runs the service.

3. Third-party work keeps its own license, beside it:
     front/vendor/three/          three.js, MIT
     front/hal/vendor/v86/        v86 (BSD-2-Clause) and SeaBIOS (LGPL-3.0)
     front/quvi/                  QuVI, MIT (see LICENSE-QuVI.txt)
     front/fonts/                 Geist and Geist Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1
   The JavaScript libraries loaded from cdnjs (Chart.js, Mermaid, anime.js) are under their own licenses.

Before 13 October 2026 the repository had no license at its root (all rights reserved), and back/rust/numbers,
back/rust/superai and back/rust/pifront declared MIT in their Cargo.toml; copies obtained under those declarations keep
the rights MIT gave them.
